quran[15]{c,v,t}:
  23,60,"and those who give (in charity) whatever they can, while their hearts are trembling with fear for they are returning to their Lord—"
  23,61,it is they who hasten towards good deeds and always take the lead in them.
  23,62,"And We do not task any soul except to the extent of its capacity, and with Us is a Book that speaks the truth, and they shall not be wronged."
  23,63,"However, their hearts are in overwhelming ignorance regarding it. Yet they have other (evil) deeds besides what they continue to do."
  23,64,"But as soon as We overtake their affluent ones with punishment, they cry for help."
  23,65,"Do not cry out today! Indeed, you will not be helped by Us."
  23,66,"Certainly, My revelations were recited to you, but you used to turn back on your heels,"
  23,67,"being arrogant to this (Book), talking nonsense in your night sessions."
  23,68,"Have they not contemplated the word (of Allah), or has something come to them which did not come to their forefathers?"
  23,69,"Or could they not recognise their Messenger, so they deny him?"
  23,70,"Or do they say: ‘There is madness in him?’ Instead, he has brought them the truth, but most of them are resentful of the truth."
  23,71,"Had the truth followed their low desires, the heavens and the earth would have surely perished along with all those in them. Rather, We have brought them their reminder, but they are disregardful of their reminder."
  23,72,"Do you ask them for any payment? Yet your Lord’s recompense is better, and He is the best of providers."
  23,73,"Surely, you invite them to a straight path."
  23,74,"Indeed, those who do not believe in the Hereafter, most certainly deviate from the path."
